# Next.js conventions

Hard locks live in `design.mdc`. Enforce them, do not restate them.

## Folders

```
app/(site)/…          routes, shared layout
components/blocks/    one folder per band (hero, features, faq…)
components/ui/        shadcn primitives, restyled to tokens
components/layout/    header, footer, nav, skip link
content/              typed copy: site.ts (name, NAP, nav, social, locales), home.ts, <page>.ts
lib/                  cn(), validators (zod), cf-image-loader.ts
public/               static assets; og.png
src/worker.ts         the small Worker for /api/* (forms) — code-cloudflare.mdc
```

cms layer: the Next.js app moves to `web/`, the Studio to `studio/` (`code-sanity.mdc`).
ecommerce layer: a server app with `app/admin/`, `app/api/`, `lib/shop/` and no Worker (`code-firebase.mdc`).

## Static export (`next.config.ts`)

```ts
const nextConfig: NextConfig = {
  output: "export",
  trailingSlash: true,                       // out/about/index.html — matches Cloudflare asset routing
  images: { loader: "custom", loaderFile: "./lib/cf-image-loader.ts" },
};
```

No route handlers, no server actions, no `dynamic = "force-dynamic"`, no middleware in a static
export — the form lives in `src/worker.ts`. Sanity data is fetched at build time.
**Layer `ecommerce` skips this section:** it is a server app (`output: "standalone"`), and
`code-firebase.mdc` owns its config.

## Rules

- Server Components by default; `"use client"` only for interaction, hooks or browser APIs, at the leaves.
- Copy never lives in JSX. `content/*.ts` (landing, multipage) or Sanity (cms).
- Every route exports `metadata`. Title ≤ 60 chars, description ≤ 155. `app/sitemap.ts`,
  `app/robots.ts`, `app/not-found.tsx` exist from `/scaffold` on.
- Images: `next/image` with explicit `width`/`height` or `fill` + aspect-ratio container; `priority`
  on the LCP image only; hero source ≤ 200 KB AVIF/WebP. Loader: Cloudflare Images for local files,
  Sanity CDN for CMS files, pre-sized WebP for shops (`code-firebase.mdc` → Images).
- Fonts: `next/font/google` or `/local`, `display: "swap"`, two families max, `font-display` and
  `font-body` tokens.
- Forms: client `zod` schema shared with the Worker; the client posts JSON to `/api/contact` with
  the Turnstile token; the Worker validates (honeypot first — `site-chrome.mdc`). Shops: the same
  order of checks, in route handlers of the same app.
- Links: `next/link` internal; `<a rel="noopener">` external; `tel:` / `mailto:` / `wa.me` from `content/site.ts`.
- i18n: Albanian + English → `app/[locale]/` with a locale list in `content/site.ts` and `hreflang`
  alternates; `generateStaticParams` for locales. One locale → no `[locale]` segment.
- Motion: `motion`, tokens for duration and easing, reduced-motion variant, ≤ 2 scroll reveals per page.
- Sticky elements: compute after mount, not with `setState` inside an effect that runs every render.
- No `any`, no `@ts-ignore`. `pnpm typecheck` = `tsc --noEmit`. ESLint ignores `out/`, `.open-next/`.
- `@playwright/test` is a dev dependency and `pnpm exec playwright install chromium` runs once in
  `/scaffold` — `/qa` scripts need it (`Cannot find module 'playwright'` shipped once).

## Before you say done

`pnpm typecheck` · `pnpm lint` · `pnpm build` (→ `out/`) · `pnpm preview` serves `out/` ·
screenshots **375 + 1440** · per-band check for bands. Shops: `pnpm test` too, and `pnpm start`
instead of `pnpm preview`.
